// Local override of upstream stm32f4.repl. Upstream models
// GPIO/USART/SPI/I2C/TIM/DMA but not Analog peripherals, so klipper's
// thermistor reads return zero and trip min_temp shutdowns on every
// printer config that has a heater - which is essentially all of them.
//
// Used by F401, F405, F407, F446 (all share stm32f4.repl in upstream).
// F429 has its own override at test/emulator/repl/stm32f429.repl
// because upstream stm32f429.repl extends stm32f4.repl with
// F429-specific bits (LTDC, FMC memory bank).
//
// This file deliberately maps NOTHING at the ADC addresses. Upstream
// omits Analog peripherals here, so 0x40012000 (ADC1) is free, and the
// renode launcher registers test/emulator/stm32_adc_stub.py there for
// the chips that need a thermistor (_AFEC_BASES_FOR_CHIP['stm32f446']).
// The Python stub (not Renode's Analog.STM32_ADC) is what completes
// klipper's F4 SR/CR2/SQR3/DR software-trigger handshake and returns
// fixture-poked conversion values - the same reason stm32f103.repl omits
// its adc1. A 0x200-byte stub window at 0x40012000 also covers ADC2
// (0x40012100, unused by klipper's F4 ADC driver, which uses ADC1 for
// every channel 0..15 and only escalates to ADC3 for channels >= 19);
// keeping any Analog model here would collide with that window. Boards
// whose thermistors land on ADC1 channels 0..15 (PA0..PC5) work as-is.
using "platforms/cpus/stm32f4.repl"
